{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun","id":1527236,"title":"Help in making archbishop encounter more fun","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-22T07:29:47-08:00","id":1527236,"title":"Help in making archbishop encounter more fun","content":"<br /> <b>edit</b>: typos :c<br /> <br /> <b>edit2</b>:<span style=\"font-size:16px\"> I really, honestly appreciate everyone's time spent answering, you're all stars; but there seems to be a general confusion about my plight. I am not looking for ideas for the Cathedral or anything cosmetic: I am looking for ideas for making <i><b>the fight</b></i> with the Tzim Archbishop more fun rather than just being a damage sponge or adding ghouls. Not getting there, specifically <i><b>fighting her</b></i>.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Long story short, we're playing V5 for almost three years now (anniversary on 1st Feb!), and my players are planning a raid on archbishop. She is new to the city, and didn't initially come to claim it, but is well-prepared, as her goal was finding and destroying a Methuselah around these parts, but then things happens, and she's now leading the crusade against the joined forces of Anarchs and Camarilla.<br /> <br /> She has a small Cathedral of Flesh, multiple twisted ghouls, and all that Tzimiche flair to her. However, I don't want them to come there and just face a lot of damage spongy monsters, and then face her war form if she even has one. This is just boring in my book, and I want to make it something special, integrating her control over her Cathedral into the battle somehow. I have a few ideas, but I worry they might be lackluster, so I was hoping to get inspiration here.<br /> <br /> Note, this is about their encounter specifically, they want to face her and kill her with their own hands - not how to get to the Cathedral itself or how they might deal with her alternatively: the players already established how they want to deal with this, and it's too late to change that c: I'm just worried the direct confrontation might be a bit being for something thus important. She's known to be a fleshcrafter and to know a little blood sorcery, but mostly relies on her pet Tremere (who is not going to be a part of confrontation - he's a desert), and to have Children she makes into fleshcrafters as well (might be an encounter as well in the Cathedral, but I'd prefer not to do that). For now I'm thinking her moving within the flesh of the walls herself while players get devoured and crushed by it instead, teeth-filled pits trying to swallow them, meat peeling off turning into tiny, but annoying ghouls, that sort of thing. Still feel it's lacking, looking for other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13437-kevintheradioguy","user":"kevintheradioguy","date":". 12-24-2023, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13437-kevintheradioguy","name":"kevintheradioguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13437_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T09:37:35-08:00","id":1527247,"title":"","content":"Some ideas that I thought of, but were never able to use, were to use some minions that looked like small spiders carrying like a bag of gastric acid, so even though the PCs could defeat them easily, they would receive damage if they got too close and this also allows for ambushes, like several If thrown from the ceiling or hidden on the back of another creature, for example, this acid could also optionally be flammable. Another idea is to make something that looks more like a very large mosquito or a modified bird that stores and injects blood into the vampire allowing a quick recharge of vitae, this gives an extra headache for the PCs and possibly a resource if desired.<br /> <br /> You mentioned that the entire cathedral is made of flesh or something like that, I don't really know the term in English, but since that's the case, how about saying that it has several fake bodies, lookalikes if you prefer, each one maintaining and linked to the original by a structure similar to a rope or cable, umbilical cord perhaps? And this sustains them with blood and allows the archbishop to give orders to each of the bodies, as well as see and hear for them and if it is damaged it is easy to replace it as you just add flesh and absorb the blood and flesh that falls during the battle, as if it were a large stomach, this creates a feeling that the PC's are not in a building, but rather inside a body. I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T09:40:40-08:00","id":1527248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun?p=1527247#post1527247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned that the entire cathedral is made of flesh or something like that</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it is a reference for a lore thing, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cathedral_of_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">Cathedral of Flesh</a>. It's not as big, but the spirit's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13437-kevintheradioguy","name":"kevintheradioguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13437_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T12:26:23-08:00","id":1527260,"title":"","content":"I would deal with the psychologic. The enticing sound of a heartbeat, the smell of blood permeating everything, curtains of skin that try to touch on the people, teeth moving in spirals up and down the columns. The whole damn thing seems to think like a single organism, half mad and half curious, in pain but actually enjoying it. Letters tattooed move around, spelling secrets of cells and organs, most to disgruntled to be understood. Stones may appear, or bone, is hard to say. Is malevolent, but so confused. Sometimes, a row of eyes fix on the members, asking if they're alive or supposed to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T13:08:21-08:00","id":1527263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun?p=1527260#post1527260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would deal with the psychologic. The enticing sound of a heartbeat, the smell of blood permeating everything, curtains of skin that try to touch on the people, teeth moving in spirals up and down the columns. The whole damn thing seems to think like a single organism, half mad and half curious, in pain but actually enjoying it. Letters tattooed move around, spelling secrets of cells and organs, most to disgruntled to be understood. Stones may appear, or bone, is hard to say. Is malevolent, but so confused. Sometimes, a row of eyes fix on the members, asking if they're alive or supposed to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh the Cathedral isn't an issue, I have a lot of gruesome things to show, being a horror DM myself. Must have not made this clear in the opening post, I'm sorry, I'll see if I can rephrase the topic somehow and edit it to be more coherent. Thing is, I have no issue with describing a Cathedral - I am concerned about the fight with the bishop - that it won't be too exciting, and my ideas about how to flare it seem a bit lacklustre imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13437-kevintheradioguy","name":"kevintheradioguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13437_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T22:43:38-08:00","id":1527287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kevintheradioguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun#post1527236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping to get inspiration here.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in doubt and have a Tzimisce?<br /> Just shamelessly rip-off Dead Space (from the maddening Marker signal as a Vicissitude/Dementation side effect to the szlachta- and vhozd-like Necromorphs)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T17:55:02-08:00","id":1527338,"title":"","content":"So I have a couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> First of all, the size/structure of the Cathedral itself can provide you with opportunities. Depending on how much space/how many chambers are within, you can potentially use a combination of cathedral architecture and human anatomy to inspire the design; the interior will help determine defensive tactics, at a minimum.<br /> <br /> (Side note: unless this Tzimisce is pretty close to a Methuselah herself, even a lesser version of the Cathedral of Flesh should probably be beyond her. It's not just the size, but the high level of Vicissitude required, pre-V5 at least. Your table, but that's my honest opinion.)<br /> <br /> Secondly, getting into the specifics of what you mean by &quot;Tzimisce flair&quot; is really important. Each Metamorphosist Tzimisce is their own Magnum Opus, the embodiment of their personal ideas of what it means to become a superior predator. Her particular abilities are going to be a reflection of that philosophy as well. Also, we need to know what tricks she is already bringing to the table before suggesting other options!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T01:05:36-08:00","id":1527350,"title":"","content":"What kind of Blood Sorcery is it that the Bishop knows? Are we talking Koldun or Thaumaturgy learnt from her pet Tremere? Or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T12:48:58-08:00","id":1527391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun?p=1527350#post1527350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of Blood Sorcery is it that the Bishop knows? Are we talking Koldun or Thaumaturgy learnt from her pet Tremere? Or something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's V5, there is only one kind of Blood Sorcery. I would've loved to use the Blood Sigil for the koldunic variation, however, I want to keep that for a bit later, for another NPC. <br /> <br /> That said, I never limit my NPCs for what's in the book. My rule of thumb is, what's in the book is exclusive to the players so they can feel special. For NPC powers, I might get inspiration from the book, but usually homebrew their abilities based off personality and overall character, so I could technically add pretty much anything that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13437-kevintheradioguy","name":"kevintheradioguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13437_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T21:19:11-08:00","id":1527452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kevintheradioguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527236-help-in-making-archbishop-encounter-more-fun?p=1527391#post1527391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's V5, there is only one kind of Blood Sorcery. I would've loved to use the Blood Sigil for the koldunic variation, however, I want to keep that for a bit later, for another NPC.<br /> <br /> That said, I never limit my NPCs for what's in the book. My rule of thumb is, what's in the book is exclusive to the players so they can feel special. For NPC powers, I might get inspiration from the book, but usually homebrew their abilities based off personality and overall character, so I could technically add pretty much anything that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing things up regarding the Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> One idea is that the bishop might have support coming in.<br /> <br /> The players would know that its only matter of time before one pack or another shows up to lend the bishop a hand against the attackers and thus the players don't have unlimited time to take down bishop. No, the bishop can't just call on help and expect everyone to drop whatever they do and come to her aid. BUT given the vinculum of the Sabbat its unliekly that all Sabbat will just leave their bishop to die at the hands of some Camarilla/Anarch punks if they get a call of assistance against an attack.<br /> <br /> Thus the encounter might have a clock ticking down so the players will have a certain time window during which they'll need to finish the bishop and escape unless they want a far harder fight on their hands.<br /> <br /> Combine this with shenaningans by the Cathedral of Flesh to buy the time needed for the incoming Sabbat pack and you might have a part that could make this fight more than just another midnight brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}